From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Hide the concurrentqueue useless-cast pragma from R CMD check

The concurrentqueue update in duckdb/duckdb#28674 wraps the cast in
hash_thread_id() in `#pragma GCC diagnostic ignored "-Wuseless-cast"`
(GCC only, between a push and a pop). R CMD check flags the file twice:
as a pragma suppressing diagnostics, and as a non-portable one, since
-Wuseless-cast is on R's list of non-portable warning flags. Its scan
matches `#pragma GCC diagnostic ignored` with single spaces; the push,
the pop and the MSVC `#pragma warning` blocks are not flagged.

Respace the one flagged line, as patch 0016 does for mbedtls, so the
compiler still honors it and the code compiles exactly as before.

Carried here until upstream takes it; not proposed upstream yet.
---
 src/duckdb/third_party/concurrentqueue/concurrentqueue.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/duckdb/third_party/concurrentqueue/concurrentqueue.h b/src/duckdb/third_party/concurrentqueue/concurrentqueue.h
--- a/src/duckdb/third_party/concurrentqueue/concurrentqueue.h
+++ b/src/duckdb/third_party/concurrentqueue/concurrentqueue.h
@@ -460,7 +460,7 @@ namespace details
 		static_assert(sizeof(thread_id_t) <= 8, "Expected a platform where thread IDs are at most 64-bit values");
 #if defined(__GNUC__) && !defined(__clang__)
 #pragma GCC diagnostic push
-#pragma GCC diagnostic ignored "-Wuseless-cast"
+#pragma  GCC  diagnostic  ignored "-Wuseless-cast"
 #endif
 		return static_cast<size_t>(hash_32_or_64<sizeof(thread_id_converter<thread_id_t>::thread_id_hash_t)>::hash(
 			thread_id_converter<thread_id_t>::prehash(id)));
